    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Intake\n\nA public n8n form collects the lead. The Set node renames form labels to stable snake_case keys (lead_name, lead_email, ...) so the rest of the workflow never depends on form wording. Swap the Form Trigger for a Webhook node if leads come from your own site.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 460
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-80, 60],
      "id": "b71f2a10-0010-4b7e-9a3d-1a2b3c4d0010",
      "name": "Note: Intake"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Claude triage\n\nHTTP Request calls the Anthropic Messages API (model: claude-sonnet-5). Retry is ON: 3 tries, 5 s apart, for transient 429/500/529 errors. The request body is built with JSON.stringify so quotes and newlines in the lead message cannot break the JSON. The Code node enforces the output contract: valid JSON, category from a fixed list.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 500
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [440, 60],
      "id": "b71f2a10-0011-4b7e-9a3d-1a2b3c4d0011",
      "name": "Note: Claude Triage"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Human approval\n\nGmail sends the classification and draft to a reviewer and pauses the workflow until they click Approve or Reject. Nothing generated by the model is stored or sent onward without this sign-off. Replace reviewer@example.com with your address.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 480
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1000, 60],
      "id": "b71f2a10-0012-4b7e-9a3d-1a2b3c4d0012",
      "name": "Note: Human Approval"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Record\n\nApproved leads are appended to a Google Sheet with the full classification and draft. Swap this node for your CRM's n8n node (HubSpot, Pipedrive, Airtable, ...) - the fields are already normalized.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 340
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1520, 60],
      "id": "b71f2a10-0013-4b7e-9a3d-1a2b3c4d0013",
      "name": "Note: Record"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Failure alerting\n\nBoth the API call and the parser route failures here instead of dying silently. Slack gets one message per failed run, and the execution stays in the n8n log so it can be inspected and retried. Point this at your own alert channel, or replace with an email node.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 500
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [440, 580],
      "id": "b71f2a10-0014-4b7e-9a3d-1a2b3c4d0014",
      "name": "Note: Failure Alerting"
    }
  ],
